Probavi brand assets — Terms of use

Copyright (c) 2026 Probavi. All rights reserved.

This repository is public so that the Probavi project, its documentation, and its
users can reference the marks correctly. It is NOT open source, and no open source
licence applies to its contents.

The Apache License 2.0 (or any other licence) that covers Probavi software does NOT
extend to the contents of this repository. Software licences grant rights to code,
not to names, logos, or trade dress.

WHAT IS RESERVED

The name "Probavi", the Probavi wordmark, the seal icon (dashed ring enclosing a
checkmark), the "Proven by Probavi" badge, and all files in this repository are
proprietary marks of the Probavi project.

PERMITTED WITHOUT ASKING

1. Referring to Probavi by name in articles, talks, documentation, and comparisons.
2. Displaying the unmodified logo to identify Probavi when writing or speaking about
   the project, in accordance with BRAND_GUIDE.md (clearspace, minimum size, no
   recolouring, no distortion).
3. Using the "Proven by Probavi" badge on a status, trust, or documentation page —
   ONLY where Probavi drills are actually configured, running, and passing. The badge
   is a factual claim about your systems. Displaying it otherwise is misrepresentation.
4. Contributors to Probavi using the marks in project-related materials.

NOT PERMITTED

1. Using the marks, or anything confusingly similar, as the name, logo, or branding
   of your own product, service, company, domain, or software distribution.
2. Modifying the marks: recolouring outside the documented palette, altering the
   geometry, adding effects, or combining them with other marks.
3. Using the marks in a way that suggests endorsement, affiliation, certification, or
   partnership that does not exist.
4. Selling merchandise or materials bearing the marks.
5. Registering the marks, or confusingly similar marks, as trademarks or domains.

FORKS AND DERIVATIVE SOFTWARE

You may fork and redistribute Probavi software under its own licence, but you may not
distribute it under the Probavi name or with Probavi branding. Remove or replace these
assets in any redistributed or modified build. This is the standard practice that keeps
"Probavi" meaningful: a user who sees the mark should know what they are getting.

QUESTIONS

For uses not covered here — press coverage, conference materials, partner pages —
open an issue in this repository.

These terms may be updated. Nothing here is legal advice.
